{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539819-how-would-having-suzaku-as-a-totem-affect-a-caern","id":1539819,"title":"How would having Suzaku as a totem affect a Caern?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-04T20:20:54-07:00","id":1539819,"title":"How would having Suzaku as a totem affect a Caern?","content":"So Suzaku can give you a +1 Pure Breed. It specifically says that she distills your bloodline into a stronger one. How would having her as a Caern totem affect the Pure Breed ratings of the kinfolk and cubs born to the sept. Is there anyway they CAN make sure that the blessings pass on to another generation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T12:55:02-07:00","id":1539875,"title":"","content":"Which Caern mechanics are you using?<br /> <br /> Assuming you're using the W20 Rage Across the World ones... first remember that the book says to modify pack Totems because no all bonuses work well as Caern Totems.<br /> <br /> Second, as I mentioned in the other thread about this, the bonuses aren't like pack Totems where some are &quot;always on.&quot; Caern spirits grant a short lived bonuses. +1 Purebreed would only really help in two major circumstances: a night with a lot of formal challenges (though that's a wash for Sept members if they're all getting +1, it could be useful if the Sept is facing challenges because other Garou think they can't handle protecting the Caern), or if everyone tries to make babies on the same night.<br /> <br /> I'd personally swap that out for a Suzaku specific variant of the Notable Heritage Merit as the bonus instead. It's far less niche but keeps to the themes fairly well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T14:01:26-07:00","id":1539883,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that a Totem's benefits as a pack totem is not the same as a caern totem. That +1 Pure Breed is an effect of having Suzaku as a pack totem, and it goes away if that Garou leaves the pack. Those powers are not permanent.<br /> <br /> I would even argue that an ST might decide to purely go with the rules of the Background as written in the corebook which is about social benefits, not the extended rules of how Pure Breed may affect offspring. Very often, the writers do not consider all the things found in all the books in terms of how it impacts mechanics. And there is a pretty steep ban associated with keeping Suzaku happy - spending at least 1/3 of all XP on improving social skills can be very restrictive - so Garou may not want to remain in such a pack for long.<br /> <br /> The powers of a caern totem - meaning any ambient magic that may be affecting the caern and the special powers obtained through Opening the caern - are more dependent on the type of caern it is. So unless the caern is associated with something like fertility or something else associated with the concept of Pure Breed, there might not be any impact to the Pure Breed of the Garou or kinfolk around the caern which has Suzaku as its caern totem.<br /> <br /> If I were the ST, I would not have some permanent bonus to Pure Breed at all. If the caern has something to do with social rolls, there'd probably some general benefit to social bonuses by opening the caern and that's it. If the caern has something to do with fertility, I'd probably limit any potential benefit to offspring be limited to opening the caern and thus not generally available to the members at large. Only those who specifically get to use its power that day. (I'd also probably make such a caern something controlled by Silver Fangs who would be desperate to control it). If it is another type of caern that somehow happens to have Suzaku, I might not have any benefit associated with the powers of Pure Breed, but limit it to more flavor text descriptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T15:37:54-07:00","id":1539892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539819-how-would-having-suzaku-as-a-totem-affect-a-caern?p=1539875#post1539875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which Caern mechanics are you using?<br /> <br /> Second, as I mentioned in the other thread about this, the bonuses aren't like pack Totems where some are &quot;always on.&quot; Caern spirits grant a short lived bonuses. +1 Purebreed would only really help in two major circumstances: a night with a lot of formal challenges (though that's a wash for Sept members if they're all getting +1, it could be useful if the Sept is facing challenges because other Garou think they can't handle protecting the Caern), or if everyone tries to make babies on the same night.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought I remembered somewhere that Caern totems can keep up the bonuses longer than usual sometimes, but they usually demand a hefty sacrifice of Gnosis. And Purebreed can boost the odds of a Garou or Kinfolk breeding true. And these are benefits that pass on to the next generation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T19:12:41-07:00","id":1539909,"title":"","content":"A Caern where once a month everybody has +1 effective PB for the sake of chance of breeding true, that's by itself huge in the setting. Such a Caern would be sought out by others for the benefits of this single night, it would either be highly disputed or well paid, and would be all the more powerful for the number of extra Garou.<br /> <br /> Imbuing this bonus on the next generation as permanent extra PB is simply too much. That's neither how a Caern Totem bonus work, nor necessary to make this Caern special.<br /> <br /> You can still do it without much concern, as the effect is purely in the setting and has zero impact on game balance, but as far as the presented question goes, that's not how anything was meant to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T20:11:23-07:00","id":1539912,"title":"","content":"Ok, that makes sense. Do you think there could be an ambient effect from having Suzaku so strong and close by? Maybe there is a higher probability of a cub or kinfolk manifesting Pure Breed, since what is practically the goddess of the phenomenon is also the goddess of the land you are living on?<br /> <br /> Not a HUGE difference, but the odds slant better in those born and raised in or by the Caern?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}